<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Nizam Shah I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1510</span> · Also known as Malik Ahmad Nizam Shah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Nizam Shah I was the founder of the Nizam Shahi dynasty and the Ahmadnagar Sultanate in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. The son of a Bahmani minister, he defeated a Bahmani army in 1490 and declared his independence, one of the breakaways that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>. In 1494 he founded the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadnagar">Ahmadnagar</a> as his capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmad-nizam-shah-i.jpg" alt="Ahmad Nizam Shah I" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kiranpawar3210 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ahmad_Nizam_Shah_Tomb_interior_with_grave.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
